{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793681971,"nonce":"b2qYQ7MB2ROuhtxHDKO7uXuH8Hg=","title":"A switch statement with both default: and case _: fails translation","message":"Found by the M4 code review (correctness reviewer). Listed under \"Not addressed here\" in https://github.com/icosahedron/csharp-ansatz/pull/1. Parent epic: `54c6e06f383039f9758f1571999c683db1c244561561998cf9a52c41b84fa52f`.\n\nExtraction lowers both `default:` and `case _:` to a discard pattern, so translation cannot tell them apart. In a switch statement that has both, translation throws `unsupported pattern DiscardPattern` (`src/Warrant.Semantics/Switches.cs`), and the unit fails instead of being translated or rejected by name.\n\nThis fails but is not unsound: no proof is produced. Ordering is otherwise right: arms run in source order, with `default` last.\n\nFix:\n\n- Reject the shape in extraction with a named WRT0002 construct, as `switch section mixing default with case labels` already is.\n- Or lower `case _:` as the catch-all it is, and treat `default:` after it as unreachable.\n\nAdd a rejected-corpus member or an extraction test either way.","files":null}]}